WEBVTT

1
00:01:32.449 --> 00:01:34.617
Tina.

2
00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.583
Tina.

3
00:01:46.841 --> 00:01:48.591
Tina.

4
00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:46.069
Tina. Tina.

5
00:03:37.982 --> 00:03:39.275
You okay. Tina?

6
00:03:40.276 --> 00:03:41.904
Just a dream. Ma.

7
00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:44.907
Some dream. judging from that.

8
00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:55.001
- You coming back to the sack or what?
- Hold your horses.

9
00:03:58.965 --> 00:04:00.800
Tina. honey. you gotta
cut your fingernails

10
00:04:00.925 --> 00:04:02.969
or you gotta stop that kind of dreaming.

11
00:04:03.094 --> 00:04:04.804
One or the other.

12
00:04:14.078 --> 00:04:19.583
One. two
Freddy's coming for you

13
00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:24.590
Three. four
Better lock your door

14
00:04:24.757 --> 00:04:29.511
Five. six
Grab your crucifix

15
00:04:29.679 --> 00:04:34.183
Seven. eight
Gonna stay up late

16
00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:37.728
Nine. 10
Never sleep again

17
00:04:37.896 --> 00:04:39.855
It was so scary.

18
00:04:40.565 --> 00:04:43.108
When I woke up. it seemed like he was
still in the room.

19
00:04:43.276 --> 00:04:46.987
Sounds like a real boogeyman.
"One. two. Freddy's coming for you."

20
00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.116
That's what it reminded me of:
that old jump-rope song.

21
00:04:50.284 --> 00:04:52.827
The worst nightmare I ever had.
You wouldn't believe it.

22
00:04:52.995 --> 00:04:55.496
Matter of fact.
I had a bad dream last night myself.

23
00:04:55.664 --> 00:04:58.166
I had a hard-on this morning
when I woke up. Tina.

24
00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:01.794
- Had your name written all over it.
- There's four letters in my name. Rod.

25
00:05:01.962 --> 00:05:04.130
How could there be room
on your joint for four letters?

26
00:05:05.466 --> 00:05:08.134
Hey. up yours
with a twirling lawn mower.

27
00:05:08.302 --> 00:05:10.136
Nyah! Rod says the sweetest things.

28
00:05:10.304 --> 00:05:12.055
- Oh. he's nuts about you.
- Yeah. nuts.

29
00:05:12.223 --> 00:05:15.810
Anyway. I couldn't go
back to sleep last night.

30
00:05:16.854 --> 00:05:18.980
- So. what did you dream?
- Forget it. Tina.

31
00:05:19.148 --> 00:05:21.858
The point is that everyone
has a bad dream once in a while.

32
00:05:22.026 --> 00:05:23.318
It's no biggie.

33
00:05:23.486 --> 00:05:26.321
Just tell yourself that's all it is
while you're having it.

34
00:05:26.489 --> 00:05:30.992
Once you do that. you wake right up.
At least it works for me.

35
00:05:34.372 --> 00:05:36.289
Hey! Did you have a nightmare too?

36
00:05:40.462 --> 00:05:45.841
Maybe we're gonna have a big earthquake.
They say things get really weird just before.

37
00:05:52.182 --> 00:05:54.267
I'm so glad you guys
could come over tonight.

38
00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:57.228
When Mom said she was taking off
for two days. I almost died.

39
00:05:57.396 --> 00:06:00.189
No problem. Tina.
Nancy and Glen to the rescue.

40
00:06:01.692 --> 00:06:04.026
Can't believe his mother's letting him
spend the night.

41
00:06:04.194 --> 00:06:08.240
Right. well. she's not. exactly.

42
00:06:08.408 --> 00:06:12.370
I got this cousin who lives near the airport.
It's okay for me to stay with him.

43
00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:14.914
And I got this sound-effects tape
from Rod. and...

44
00:06:15.082 --> 00:06:16.958
Hello. Mom?

45
00:06:17.876 --> 00:06:20.670
Yeah. Out here at Barry's.

46
00:06:23.507 --> 00:06:27.010
Huh? Yeah. noisy as usual.
Glad we don't live here. huh?

47
00:06:27.928 --> 00:06:30.471
Yeah. Aunt Eunice says hello.

48
00:06:31.056 --> 00:06:34.476
Right. right. I'll call you in the morning.
Yeah. Yeah. sure...

49
00:06:37.731 --> 00:06:39.898
Just some kids drag-racing outside.
I think. Mom.

50
00:06:42.694 --> 00:06:44.945
Listen. Ma. I gotta go.
I think there's been an accident out front.

51
00:06:47.198 --> 00:06:48.240
Right.

52
00:06:50.368 --> 00:06:52.286
All right. I'll call the police.

53
00:06:53.163 --> 00:06:55.581
Right. I'll call the police.

54
00:06:55.749 --> 00:06:57.041
uh...

55
00:06:57.208 --> 00:06:59.586
No. Just some neighbors
having a fight. I guess.

56
00:06:59.754 --> 00:07:01.921
I'll call you in the morning.

57
00:07:09.139 --> 00:07:10.348
It worked like a charm.

58
00:07:10.515 --> 00:07:11.766
Smooth.

59
00:07:11.933 --> 00:07:12.975
Jesus.

60
00:07:14.978 --> 00:07:17.438
See? I told you you'd be feeling better.

61
00:07:18.774 --> 00:07:22.610
All day long.
I've been seeing that guy's weird face...

62
00:07:22.778 --> 00:07:24.738
...and hearing those fingernails.

63
00:07:25.156 --> 00:07:27.199
Fingernails?

64
00:07:27.367 --> 00:07:29.117
That's amazing. you saying that.

65
00:07:29.285 --> 00:07:32.621
That made me remember
the dream I had last night.

66
00:07:32.789 --> 00:07:34.289
What did you dream?

67
00:07:34.457 --> 00:07:38.293
I dreamed about a guy
in a dirty red and green sweater.

68
00:07:39.921 --> 00:07:42.381
Well. what about the fingernails?

69
00:07:43.883 --> 00:07:46.968
Oh. he scraped
his fingernails along things.

70
00:07:47.136 --> 00:07:49.805
Actually. they were more like
finger-knives or something.

71
00:07:49.973 --> 00:07:53.518
Something he made himself.
but they made a horrible sound.

72
00:07:54.103 --> 00:07:55.353
It was like:

73
00:07:57.106 --> 00:08:02.319
Nancy. you dreamed
about the same creep I did.

74
00:08:03.279 --> 00:08:04.863
That's impossible.

75
00:08:07.659 --> 00:08:08.659
What?

76
00:08:09.953 --> 00:08:11.662
Nothing.

77
00:08:11.830 --> 00:08:15.833
- There's something out there. isn't there?
- I didn't hear anything.

78
00:08:16.001 --> 00:08:18.837
Well. I heard something.

79
00:08:52.456 --> 00:08:56.042
I'm gonna punch out your ugly lights.
whoever you are.

80
00:08:59.964 --> 00:09:01.339
Kitty. kitty.

81
00:09:08.724 --> 00:09:10.558
Chow. chow. chow.

82
00:09:16.398 --> 00:09:20.359
It's Rod Lane bringing Lantz down
just three yards from the goal line!

83
00:09:20.527 --> 00:09:23.070
What a brilliant tackle.
and the fans go wild.

84
00:09:23.238 --> 00:09:27.575
- What the hell are you doing here?
- Came to make up. No big deal.

85
00:09:27.743 --> 00:09:30.495
- Your mom home?
- Course.

86
00:09:30.662 --> 00:09:33.456
- Oh. what's that?
- Intense. huh?

87
00:09:37.504 --> 00:09:39.671
So. what's going on here.
an orgy or something?

88
00:09:39.839 --> 00:09:41.590
Maybe a funeral. dickhead.

89
00:09:42.258 --> 00:09:44.176
It's just a sleepover date. Rod.

90
00:09:44.344 --> 00:09:47.304
Tina and me. Glen was just leaving.

91
00:09:49.642 --> 00:09:52.101
- You see his face?
- "You see his face?"

92
00:09:53.103 --> 00:09:55.605
Your mom ain't home. is she?

93
00:09:55.773 --> 00:09:58.358
Me and Tina got stuff to discuss.

94
00:09:58.526 --> 00:10:00.110
Rod.

95
00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.824
We got her mother's bed.
You guys got the rest.

96
00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:11.997
I think we should get out of here.

97
00:10:12.791 --> 00:10:14.959
Hey. you guys are gonna
hang around. right?

98
00:10:15.460 --> 00:10:17.920
I mean. don't leave me alone
with this lunatic.

99
00:10:18.088 --> 00:10:19.463
Please. Nancy?

100
00:10:25.929 --> 00:10:28.723
Glen. not now.

101
00:10:29.767 --> 00:10:32.310
We're here for Tina now. not ourselves.

102
00:10:36.107 --> 00:10:38.525
Why is she so bothered
by a stupid nightmare. anyway?

103
00:10:38.693 --> 00:10:41.736
Because he was scary. that's why.

104
00:10:58.840 --> 00:11:00.257
Yeah.

105
00:11:04.095 --> 00:11:05.345
Oh. Rod!

106
00:11:06.556 --> 00:11:08.015
Yeah. Yeah. Tina!

107
00:11:10.018 --> 00:11:12.352
Oh. God! Oh. God!

108
00:11:14.689 --> 00:11:16.106
Oh. God!

109
00:11:16.274 --> 00:11:19.027
Oh. God! Oh. Rod!

110
00:11:21.822 --> 00:11:24.157
Morality sucks.

111
00:11:35.919 --> 00:11:38.547
I knew there was something about you
I liked.

112
00:11:39.382 --> 00:11:42.718
- You feel better now. right?
- Jungle man fix Jane.

113
00:11:44.347 --> 00:11:45.722
No more fights?

114
00:11:47.975 --> 00:11:49.059
No more fights.

115
00:11:49.226 --> 00:11:51.061
Good.

116
00:11:51.228 --> 00:11:53.772
No more nightmares
for either one of us. then.

117
00:11:55.566 --> 00:11:58.193
When did you have a nightmare?

118
00:12:00.571 --> 00:12:02.906
Guys can have nightmares too.
you know.

119
00:12:03.491 --> 00:12:06.076
You ain't got a corner
on the market or something.

120
00:13:07.058 --> 00:13:08.100
Rod?

121
00:13:14.190 --> 00:13:16.650
Tina.

122
00:13:40.886 --> 00:13:42.720
Tina.

123
00:13:44.473 --> 00:13:47.099
Who do you think you are?

124
00:13:48.018 --> 00:13:50.311
Whoever you are.

125
00:15:01.178 --> 00:15:02.804
Somebody there?

126
00:15:02.972 --> 00:15:04.806
Tina.

127
00:15:22.702 --> 00:15:24.452
Tina.

128
00:15:24.996 --> 00:15:27.122
Who the hell is that?

129
00:15:52.316 --> 00:15:53.649
Tina.

130
00:15:55.319 --> 00:15:57.153
Shit.

131
00:16:06.873 --> 00:16:08.040
Please. God...

132
00:16:08.207 --> 00:16:10.043
This...

133
00:16:10.210 --> 00:16:11.377
...is God.

134
00:16:20.679 --> 00:16:24.307
No! No! No!

135
00:16:25.351 --> 00:16:27.060
Yes!

136
00:16:30.607 --> 00:16:32.483
Tina!

137
00:16:34.152 --> 00:16:35.277
Watch this.

138
00:16:45.830 --> 00:16:48.415
Nancy! Open the door!

139
00:16:48.583 --> 00:16:50.376
Nancy!

140
00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:07.561
Rod. help me! Oh. God!

141
00:17:07.729 --> 00:17:09.689
No! No!

142
00:17:09.856 --> 00:17:11.357
Help me. Rod!

143
00:17:11.525 --> 00:17:14.735
Help me! Rod! Rod!

144
00:17:15.654 --> 00:17:19.240
- Help me!
- Tina!

145
00:17:38.428 --> 00:17:40.053
Tina!

146
00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:44.850
Tina! Tina!

147
00:17:45.018 --> 00:17:47.310
Tina!

148
00:17:47.729 --> 00:17:51.441
- Tina!
- Rod! Rod!

149
00:17:53.485 --> 00:17:55.278
Tina!

150
00:18:00.744 --> 00:18:03.454
- Tina? Tina?
- Who did this? I'll kill you.

151
00:18:03.621 --> 00:18:06.540
- Who did this?
- Aaagh! Oh. God. you scared me!

152
00:18:24.643 --> 00:18:25.685
What have you got?

153
00:18:25.853 --> 00:18:28.313
Her name was Tina Gray.
It's her home.

154
00:18:28.481 --> 00:18:31.608
Father abandoned 10 years ago.
mother's in Vegas with her boyfriend.

155
00:18:31.776 --> 00:18:34.152
- We're trying to reach her.
- What's the coroner got?

156
00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:38.656
Something like a razor was the weapon.
but nothing was found at the scene.

157
00:18:39.158 --> 00:18:40.868
It looks like the victim's boyfriend.

158
00:18:41.036 --> 00:18:42.244
- Lieutenant.
- Where is she?

159
00:18:42.412 --> 00:18:46.499
- I put her in your office.
- His name's Rod Lane. He's a musician type.

160
00:18:46.666 --> 00:18:51.170
- Arrests for drugs. brawling.
- Terrific. What the hell was she doing there?

161
00:18:51.338 --> 00:18:52.338
She lived there.

162
00:18:53.424 --> 00:18:55.550
I don't mean her.

163
00:18:56.427 --> 00:18:58.595
I mean you.

164
00:18:58.763 --> 00:19:01.681
What was she doing there?

165
00:19:02.016 --> 00:19:03.934
Hello to you too. Donald.

166
00:19:04.644 --> 00:19:07.355
Marge. Okay.

167
00:19:12.194 --> 00:19:14.112
How you doing. baby?

168
00:19:14.279 --> 00:19:16.614
I'm okay. Dad.

169
00:19:17.783 --> 00:19:19.617
Look. I don't wanna
get into this now...

170
00:19:19.785 --> 00:19:22.537
...God knows you need time.
but I sure would like to know...

171
00:19:22.704 --> 00:19:26.874
...what the hell you were doing shacking up
with three kids in the middle of the night...

172
00:19:27.042 --> 00:19:29.252
...especially a lunatic delinquent
like Lane.

173
00:19:29.878 --> 00:19:32.088
Rod is not a lunatic. Dad.

174
00:19:32.256 --> 00:19:35.050
You have a sane explanation
for what he did?

175
00:19:37.303 --> 00:19:39.555
Apparently. he was crazy jealous.

176
00:19:39.722 --> 00:19:43.058
- Nancy said they'd had a fight.
- It wasn't that serious.

177
00:19:43.226 --> 00:19:45.144
Maybe you don't think murder is serious.

178
00:19:45.311 --> 00:19:48.606
How can you say I don't take
her death seriously?

179
00:19:52.111 --> 00:19:54.237
Look. all I meant...

180
00:19:56.282 --> 00:19:58.868
...was that their fights
weren't that serious.

181
00:20:03.832 --> 00:20:05.249
You know. Tina...

182
00:20:05.417 --> 00:20:07.418
...she dreamed this was gonna happen.

183
00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:10.045
What?

184
00:20:10.213 --> 00:20:15.968
She had a nightmare
that someone was trying to kill her.

185
00:20:16.386 --> 00:20:22.266
That's why we were there. Mom.
She just didn't wanna sleep alone.

186
00:20:29.066 --> 00:20:31.985
Police say the victim.
15-year-old Christina Gray...

187
00:20:32.153 --> 00:20:34.654
...had quarreled earlier
with her boyfriend. Rod Lane.

188
00:20:34.822 --> 00:20:38.158
Lane is now the subject
of a citywide manhunt.

189
00:20:38.534 --> 00:20:42.413
The murder weapon. a straight razor
or similar sharp object. has not yet...

190
00:20:45.834 --> 00:20:48.252
Where do you think you're going?

191
00:20:49.838 --> 00:20:51.131
School.

192
00:20:51.299 --> 00:20:53.592
You were tossing and turning
all night last night.

193
00:20:53.760 --> 00:20:55.969
You have no business
going to school today.

194
00:20:56.137 --> 00:20:59.932
I've gotta go to school. Mother.
Otherwise I'll sit up there and go crazy.

195
00:21:00.099 --> 00:21:02.100
Did you sleep?

196
00:21:02.936 --> 00:21:05.145
I'll sleep in study hall.

197
00:21:05.647 --> 00:21:08.482
I'd rather keep busy. you know?

198
00:21:09.525 --> 00:21:12.152
- Right home after?
- Right home after.

199
00:21:12.320 --> 00:21:13.612
Okay.

200
00:21:14.322 --> 00:21:16.740
- See you.
- See you.

201
00:21:53.447 --> 00:21:57.242
I'm not gonna hurt you.
I'm not gonna hurt you.

202
00:22:00.413 --> 00:22:03.707
- They're gonna kill me for sure.
- Nobody's gonna kill you.

203
00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:07.377
Did you do it?

204
00:22:08.879 --> 00:22:12.383
- I never touched her.
- You were screaming like crazy.

205
00:22:12.551 --> 00:22:14.385
There was somebody else there.

206
00:22:14.553 --> 00:22:16.721
The door was locked from your side.

207
00:22:16.888 --> 00:22:20.016
Don't look at me like I'm some
fucking fruitcake or something!

208
00:22:20.183 --> 00:22:23.936
- I'm warning you.
- Just move away from her. son.

209
00:22:24.104 --> 00:22:27.064
Real easy.
like your ass depended on it.

210
00:22:27.232 --> 00:22:28.566
Hold it!

211
00:22:28.734 --> 00:22:31.445
- No!
- Jesus Christ.

212
00:22:40.247 --> 00:22:41.289
Hold it right there.

213
00:22:41.457 --> 00:22:43.916
- Watch it. Hold them.
- All right. I'm cool. I'm cool.

214
00:22:44.084 --> 00:22:46.210
- Okay. I got him.
- On the ground. now.

215
00:22:46.378 --> 00:22:49.339
- Come on. Get down.
- Lieutenant. look at this. A switchblade.

216
00:22:49.506 --> 00:22:52.216
I didn't do it! I didn't kill her. Nancy!

217
00:22:52.384 --> 00:22:53.634
Daddy?

218
00:22:54.345 --> 00:22:55.762
You used me.

219
00:22:56.263 --> 00:22:59.098
What the hell were you doing
going to school today for anyway?

220
00:23:00.893 --> 00:23:02.311
Nancy.

221
00:23:02.479 --> 00:23:03.979
Nancy!

222
00:23:04.773 --> 00:23:07.274
- Nancy!
- Come on. let go of my arm.

223
00:23:07.442 --> 00:23:11.278
What is seen is not always what is real.

224
00:23:11.946 --> 00:23:16.116
According to Shakespeare.
there was something operating in nature...

225
00:23:16.576 --> 00:23:20.662
...perhaps inside human nature itself.
that was rotten.

226
00:23:21.122 --> 00:23:23.957
A canker. as he put it.

227
00:23:24.584 --> 00:23:26.961
Now. of course.
Hamlet's response to this...

228
00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:33.302
...and to his mother's lies.
was to continually probe and dig.

229
00:23:33.553 --> 00:23:36.180
Just like the gravediggers...

230
00:23:36.348 --> 00:23:39.642
...always trying to get
beneath the surface.

231
00:23:40.143 --> 00:23:44.480
The same is true in a different way
in Julius Caesar. John. go ahead. please.

232
00:23:50.612 --> 00:23:52.071
uh...

233
00:23:52.614 --> 00:23:58.161
In the most high and palmy state of Rome.
a little ere the mightiest Julius fell.

234
00:23:58.329 --> 00:24:01.248
The graves stood tenantless.
and the sheeted dead...

235
00:24:01.416 --> 00:24:04.543
...did squeak and gibber
in the Roman streets:

236
00:24:04.710 --> 00:24:07.337
As stars with trains of fire
and dews of blood...

237
00:24:07.505 --> 00:24:09.673
...disasters in the sun. and the moist star...

238
00:24:09.841 --> 00:24:12.676
...upon whose influence
Neptune's empire stands...

239
00:24:12.844 --> 00:24:15.178
Nancy.

240
00:24:18.182 --> 00:24:19.559
Nancy.

241
00:24:24.524 --> 00:24:27.860
O God! I could be bounded in a nutshell...

242
00:24:28.027 --> 00:24:31.989
...and count myself a king
of infinite space...

243
00:24:32.907 --> 00:24:37.953
...were it not that I have bad dreams.

244
00:24:58.684 --> 00:25:17.913
Tina?

245
00:25:24.462 --> 00:25:28.256
- Where's your pass?
- Screw your pass.

246
00:25:31.802 --> 00:25:33.720
Hey. Nancy.

247
00:25:34.305 --> 00:25:37.098
No running in the hallway.

248
00:25:55.953 --> 00:25:57.620
Tina?

249
00:26:25.067 --> 00:26:26.943
Tina?

250
00:26:46.881 --> 00:26:52.469
Tina?

251
00:26:58.519 --> 00:26:59.561
Who are you?

252
00:27:47.028 --> 00:27:49.072
Gonna get you.

253
00:27:58.249 --> 00:28:02.169
- It's only a dream!
- Come to Freddy.

254
00:28:02.337 --> 00:28:03.796
Goddamn you!

255
00:28:09.844 --> 00:28:12.179
No! No!

256
00:28:12.347 --> 00:28:15.684
Okay! Okay. okay! Thompson!

257
00:28:15.851 --> 00:28:18.269
I'll call your mother.

258
00:28:18.604 --> 00:28:20.772
Everything is all right now.

259
00:28:20.940 --> 00:28:23.775
- Come on. Sit down.
- No.

260
00:28:26.570 --> 00:28:29.155
I'm okay. I'm fine.

261
00:28:29.323 --> 00:28:33.034
- You sure?
- Yeah. I'll go straight home.

262
00:28:33.452 --> 00:28:36.329
You'll need a hall pass.

263
00:28:37.623 --> 00:28:38.873
uh...

264
00:28:39.041 --> 00:28:41.127
Back to work.

265
00:29:05.487 --> 00:29:07.405
God!

266
00:29:34.601 --> 00:29:38.520
- And then what happened?
- I told you.

267
00:29:39.063 --> 00:29:41.982
It was dark. but I'm sure
there was somebody in there...

268
00:29:42.150 --> 00:29:43.567
...under the covers with her.

269
00:29:44.027 --> 00:29:47.822
How could somebody be under the covers
with you without you knowing about it?

270
00:29:47.990 --> 00:29:49.866
How the fuck do I know?

271
00:29:50.201 --> 00:29:52.911
I don't expect you to believe me anyway.

272
00:29:54.914 --> 00:29:57.415
What did he look like?

273
00:29:59.169 --> 00:30:00.544
Did you get a look at him?

274
00:30:02.881 --> 00:30:04.507
No.

275
00:30:05.050 --> 00:30:08.427
Well. then how do you know
that somebody else was there?

276
00:30:09.387 --> 00:30:11.555
Because somebody cut her
while I watched.

277
00:30:12.015 --> 00:30:16.644
- And you didn't get a look at him?
- I couldn't even see the fucker.

278
00:30:16.812 --> 00:30:18.938
You could just see...

279
00:30:19.689 --> 00:30:21.899
...cuts happening...

280
00:30:22.067 --> 00:30:23.108
...all at once.

281
00:30:23.820 --> 00:30:26.363
What do you mean all at once?

282
00:30:27.573 --> 00:30:33.245
I mean. it was as if
there were four razors...

283
00:30:33.704 --> 00:30:36.581
...cutting her at the same time...

284
00:30:36.999 --> 00:30:38.917
...but invisible ones.

285
00:30:40.086 --> 00:30:43.172
You know.
I probably could have saved her...

286
00:30:44.466 --> 00:30:46.217
...if I'd have moved sooner...

287
00:30:48.303 --> 00:30:51.723
...but I thought it was
just another nightmare...

288
00:30:51.891 --> 00:30:54.810
...like the one I had the night before.

289
00:30:57.188 --> 00:31:00.107
There was this... There was this guy.

290
00:31:02.777 --> 00:31:05.612
He had knives for fingers.

291
00:31:16.250 --> 00:31:17.834
Hey. you think I did it?

292
00:31:19.962 --> 00:31:21.754
No.

293
00:31:38.356 --> 00:31:42.611
One. two
Freddy's coming for you

294
00:31:43.195 --> 00:31:48.450
Three. four
Better lock your door

295
00:31:48.659 --> 00:31:54.164
Five. six
Grab your crucifix

296
00:31:54.332 --> 00:32:00.295
Seven. eight
Gonna stay up late

297
00:32:02.256 --> 00:32:09.263
Nine. 10
Never sleep again

298
00:32:23.445 --> 00:32:26.530
- Nancy?
- What. Mother?

299
00:32:26.698 --> 00:32:28.407
Don't fall asleep in there.

300
00:32:28.575 --> 00:32:31.745
- You could drown. you know.
- Oh. for Pete's sakes.

301
00:32:31.913 --> 00:32:33.246
It happens all the time.

302
00:32:33.414 --> 00:32:35.249
I've heated up some warm milk for you.

303
00:32:35.709 --> 00:32:38.753
Warm milk? Gross.

304
00:33:10.829 --> 00:33:11.912
Help!

305
00:33:18.962 --> 00:33:20.796
Nancy!

306
00:33:27.431 --> 00:33:30.266
- Hold on. baby!
- Mom!

307
00:33:35.522 --> 00:33:36.605
I'm okay.

308
00:33:36.773 --> 00:33:39.275
- You're okay?
- I'm okay.

309
00:33:39.443 --> 00:33:41.777
But I heard you screaming.
You were calling me.

310
00:33:41.945 --> 00:33:45.573
I just slipped
getting out of the tub. Mom.

311
00:33:45.741 --> 00:33:49.285
I told you hundreds of people a year
get killed like that. honey.

312
00:33:49.453 --> 00:33:52.873
I know. but I'm okay. Mother.
I'm sorry for scaring you.

313
00:33:53.041 --> 00:33:54.583
It's okay.

314
00:33:54.751 --> 00:33:56.460
I'll turn down your bed. okay?

315
00:33:56.627 --> 00:33:58.336
All right. I'll get my pajamas on.

316
00:33:58.504 --> 00:33:59.796
Okay.

317
00:34:20.862 --> 00:34:24.239
all-consuming act
of bodily dismemberment.

318
00:34:24.783 --> 00:34:26.992
No! No!

319
00:35:02.613 --> 00:35:05.240
- Hi.
- God!

320
00:35:06.450 --> 00:35:09.244
I'm sorry. Your light was on.
I thought I'd see how you were.

321
00:35:09.411 --> 00:35:12.039
Sometimes I wish
you didn't live right across the street.

322
00:35:12.207 --> 00:35:15.293
Will you shut up and let me in?
Ever stand on a trellis in your bare feet?

323
00:35:15.461 --> 00:35:17.003
Get inside before somebody sees you.

324
00:35:17.171 --> 00:35:18.338
- Ow!
- Shh!

325
00:35:18.506 --> 00:35:19.548
I hit my head.

326
00:35:19.715 --> 00:35:22.342
Gotta be quiet.
Mom's not even asleep yet.

327
00:35:27.181 --> 00:35:28.223
If you don't mind.

328
00:35:37.234 --> 00:35:39.443
I heard you freaked out
in English class today.

329
00:35:39.611 --> 00:35:43.573
- Yeah. I guess I did.
- You haven't slept yet. have you?

330
00:35:44.700 --> 00:35:47.577
- Not really.
- What did you do to your arm?

331
00:35:48.579 --> 00:35:50.121
I burned it in English class.

332
00:35:55.419 --> 00:35:58.754
Oh. God. I look 20 years old.

333
00:36:01.925 --> 00:36:04.595
Did you have
any weird dreams last night?

334
00:36:04.762 --> 00:36:06.221
Slept like a rock.

335
00:36:06.764 --> 00:36:10.101
Do you believe that people can dream
about what's going to happen?

336
00:36:14.064 --> 00:36:16.274
- No.
- Do you believe in the boogeyman?

337
00:36:16.442 --> 00:36:17.692
No.

338
00:36:17.860 --> 00:36:20.570
Rod killed Tina. and you know that.

339
00:36:21.947 --> 00:36:23.990
I've got a crazy favor to ask you.

340
00:36:24.617 --> 00:36:26.826
- uh-oh.
- It's nothing hard or anything.

341
00:36:28.455 --> 00:36:31.457
I'm gonna go and look for somebody...

342
00:36:31.625 --> 00:36:36.462
...and I want you to stand
like a sort of a guard. okay?

343
00:36:38.173 --> 00:36:41.008
- Okay?
- Okay.

344
00:36:42.260 --> 00:36:46.472
Now. you can't mess up.
A lot might depend on this.

345
00:36:46.640 --> 00:36:48.307
I won't screw up.

346
00:36:48.808 --> 00:36:50.017
Okay. turn off the light.

347
00:36:55.191 --> 00:36:58.485
- Okay. here's what we're gonna do.
- It's dark in here.

348
00:36:59.028 --> 00:37:01.238
And it's not what you're thinking.

349
00:37:52.334 --> 00:37:54.043
Glen?

350
00:37:54.878 --> 00:37:55.920
Are you still watching?

351
00:37:58.675 --> 00:38:01.135
- Yeah. so?
- I'm just checking.

352
00:39:33.525 --> 00:39:35.317
Glen!

353
00:39:36.486 --> 00:39:38.320
Glen?

354
00:39:40.990 --> 00:39:43.075
Glen!

355
00:39:47.748 --> 00:39:52.710
Rod! Watch out! Rod! Watch out!

356
00:39:53.504 --> 00:39:55.380
Glen!

357
00:40:01.680 --> 00:40:05.850
- Glen!
- Nancy.

358
00:40:07.853 --> 00:40:10.438
Nancy.

359
00:40:19.865 --> 00:40:21.824
Glen!

360
00:40:22.743 --> 00:40:25.078
Wake up!

361
00:40:26.414 --> 00:40:28.790
Are you there?

362
00:40:28.958 --> 00:40:31.460
I'm here.

363
00:41:00.408 --> 00:41:03.785
Nancy. help me. please.

364
00:41:03.953 --> 00:41:05.704
- Save me from...
- Freddy.

365
00:41:10.710 --> 00:41:12.669
Glen!

366
00:41:17.426 --> 00:41:22.889
This is just a dream. This isn't real.
This is just a dream. He isn't real. He isn't...

367
00:41:40.701 --> 00:41:42.410
Glen!

368
00:41:46.791 --> 00:41:58.176
No!

369
00:41:58.344 --> 00:41:59.803
Glen. no!

370
00:42:13.735 --> 00:42:16.821
Glen. you bastard.

371
00:42:17.656 --> 00:42:18.823
What did I do?

372
00:42:18.991 --> 00:42:22.827
I just asked you to do one thing.
just stay awake and watch me...

373
00:42:22.995 --> 00:42:26.914
...just wake me up if it looked
like I was having a bad dream...

374
00:42:27.082 --> 00:42:31.378
...and what did you do?
You shithead. You fell asleep.

375
00:42:31.546 --> 00:42:33.006
- Nancy?
- Oh. shit.

376
00:42:34.508 --> 00:42:35.717
- Hurry.
- Ow.

377
00:42:35.884 --> 00:42:36.968
Shh.

378
00:42:37.136 --> 00:42:39.554
Shut up and stay there.
Don't go away.

379
00:42:45.352 --> 00:42:47.103
Are you okay?

380
00:42:47.521 --> 00:42:50.732
Yeah. It was just a little dream.
I'm going right back to sleep.

381
00:42:50.899 --> 00:42:53.568
Okay. Call me if you need anything. okay?

382
00:42:54.528 --> 00:42:55.570
Okay.

383
00:43:03.246 --> 00:43:04.872
Glen.

384
00:43:12.881 --> 00:43:15.883
- You mind telling me what's going on?
- Oh. just come on.

385
00:43:16.051 --> 00:43:17.051
Yeah.

386
00:43:18.094 --> 00:43:21.472
Garcia. I've gotta see Rod Lane again.

387
00:43:21.640 --> 00:43:25.019
You know. I took the night shift
so I could get some peace and quiet.

388
00:43:25.187 --> 00:43:26.395
Look. it's urgent!

389
00:43:43.330 --> 00:43:46.791
We have reason to believe there might
be something strange going on here.

390
00:43:46.958 --> 00:43:48.417
Got no argument with that.

391
00:43:49.127 --> 00:43:50.252
What are you doing here?

392
00:43:50.420 --> 00:43:53.340
There's an unsolved murder.
and I don't like unsolved murders.

393
00:43:53.508 --> 00:43:55.634
Especially ones that my daughter's
mixed up in.

394
00:43:55.802 --> 00:43:57.094
What are you doing here?

395
00:43:57.261 --> 00:44:00.972
- At this hour. you should be home in bed.
- I just wanna see if he's okay.

396
00:44:01.140 --> 00:44:04.267
Nancy. take my word for it.
The guy's sleeping like a baby.

397
00:44:04.435 --> 00:44:05.560
He's not going anywhere.

398
00:44:13.778 --> 00:44:15.612
Just go down and look at him.

399
00:44:18.325 --> 00:44:19.451
Please. Daddy.

400
00:44:21.496 --> 00:44:24.998
All right. Garcia. give me the keys.

401
00:44:25.625 --> 00:44:27.292
All right.

402
00:44:28.378 --> 00:44:30.003
Where the hell did I put the keys?

403
00:44:39.347 --> 00:44:41.306
Hey. hey!

404
00:44:48.315 --> 00:44:52.986
Help! Help! Help!

405
00:45:00.619 --> 00:45:01.995
Jesus!

406
00:45:02.788 --> 00:45:04.330
Rod!

407
00:45:08.712 --> 00:45:09.754
Hurry. Cut him down.

408
00:45:11.840 --> 00:45:13.800
- Grab his legs.
- I got him.

409
00:45:13.968 --> 00:45:15.969
God!

410
00:45:16.763 --> 00:45:19.181
Goddamn crazy kid.

411
00:45:20.099 --> 00:45:22.142
- Grab his back. would you?
- Got it.

412
00:45:22.310 --> 00:45:24.478
Lower him.

413
00:45:48.086 --> 00:45:50.880
Ashes to ashes. dust to dust.

414
00:45:51.673 --> 00:45:54.592
May God be
with this young man's soul.

415
00:45:56.136 --> 00:46:01.141
His life and his death
attest to the scriptures' warning...

416
00:46:01.351 --> 00:46:04.728
...that he who lives by the sword
shall die by the sword.

417
00:46:06.397 --> 00:46:10.235
But let us recall also
our Lord's admonition...

418
00:46:10.402 --> 00:46:14.280
...that we judge not. lest we be judged.

419
00:46:15.157 --> 00:46:17.283
And may Rod Lane rest in peace.

420
00:46:23.123 --> 00:46:25.416
Time to go. honey.

421
00:46:31.716 --> 00:46:33.425
Hop in.

422
00:46:36.263 --> 00:46:37.930
The killer's still loose. you know.

423
00:46:39.182 --> 00:46:42.434
You're saying somebody else
killed Tina. Who?

424
00:46:43.436 --> 00:46:45.813
I don't know who he is...

425
00:46:46.523 --> 00:46:50.150
...but he's burned.
and he wears a weird hat...

426
00:46:51.570 --> 00:46:54.823
...and a red and green sweater.
really dirty...

427
00:46:54.991 --> 00:46:59.619
...and he uses these knives.
like giant fingernails.

428
00:47:02.958 --> 00:47:06.961
Better keep her home for a few days.
until she gets over the shock of this.

429
00:47:07.129 --> 00:47:10.464
I've got something better.
I'm going to get her some help.

430
00:47:35.491 --> 00:47:39.036
I don't see why you couldn't just
give me a pill to keep me from dreaming.

431
00:47:39.203 --> 00:47:43.123
Everyone's got to dream. young lady.
If you don't dream. you go.

432
00:47:44.208 --> 00:47:46.377
Okay. all set?

433
00:47:47.212 --> 00:47:51.341
- No.
- Please. Nancy. trust us.

434
00:47:51.508 --> 00:47:54.677
It's not you I don't trust. It's just...

435
00:48:00.018 --> 00:48:01.977
Okay.

436
00:48:03.021 --> 00:48:05.022
Let's do it.

437
00:48:10.905 --> 00:48:13.031
- Thank you. nurse.
Mm-hm.

438
00:48:29.924 --> 00:48:33.551
How long has this been going on?
- Since the murders.

439
00:48:33.719 --> 00:48:35.804
She was fine before that.

440
00:48:36.430 --> 00:48:38.307
Now she thinks her dreams are real.

441
00:48:38.475 --> 00:48:42.478
Well. there's no sign of pathology
in her EEG.

442
00:48:42.646 --> 00:48:45.064
I'd guess that what we have
is just a normal girl...

443
00:48:45.232 --> 00:48:48.067
...who happens to have gone
through two days of hell.

444
00:48:54.909 --> 00:48:56.243
Okay.

445
00:48:57.412 --> 00:48:58.745
She's asleep now.

446
00:48:59.580 --> 00:49:00.914
Thank God.

447
00:49:04.294 --> 00:49:07.255
What the hell are dreams anyway?

448
00:49:07.589 --> 00:49:10.717
Mysteries. Incredible body hocus-pocus.

449
00:49:10.884 --> 00:49:16.305
The truth is we still don't know
what they are or where they come from.

450
00:49:22.980 --> 00:49:27.650
Okay. She's going into deep sleep now.

451
00:49:29.946 --> 00:49:33.115
Heart rate is a little high.
It's just due to anxiety.

452
00:49:33.283 --> 00:49:35.951
Otherwise she's nicely relaxed.

453
00:49:36.119 --> 00:49:40.456
All signs are normal.
She could dream at any time now.

454
00:49:44.252 --> 00:49:46.171
Beta waves are slowing.

455
00:49:50.968 --> 00:49:53.636
She's into REMs now.

456
00:49:54.013 --> 00:49:56.974
She's definitely dreaming now.

457
00:49:57.142 --> 00:50:00.811
It's a good one too.
Typical dream parameter.

458
00:50:01.438 --> 00:50:06.067
A nightmare now
would be plus or minus five or six.

459
00:50:06.693 --> 00:50:09.403
She's about three.

460
00:50:16.495 --> 00:50:18.829
- Doctor. what's she doing now?
- I'm not...

461
00:50:18.997 --> 00:50:20.164
Is she asleep or awake?

462
00:50:20.332 --> 00:50:22.709
Something's wrong.
It never gets this high.

463
00:50:23.836 --> 00:50:26.254
- What's she doing?
- I don't know.

464
00:50:26.422 --> 00:50:27.714
Is she dreaming?

465
00:50:34.639 --> 00:50:37.015
- Listen...
- Nancy! Nancy. it's Mom. it's Mom.

466
00:50:37.183 --> 00:50:38.350
Nancy. It's Mom.

467
00:50:42.272 --> 00:50:44.982
What? Her hair.

468
00:50:45.150 --> 00:50:47.236
- Excuse me.
- This'll help you sleep.

469
00:50:48.196 --> 00:50:50.030
No!

470
00:50:50.198 --> 00:50:52.699
Oh. my God. her arm!
Get something.

471
00:50:54.077 --> 00:50:56.328
What happened. baby? What happened?

472
00:50:59.707 --> 00:51:02.126
It's okay. it's okay.

473
00:51:04.254 --> 00:51:07.047
I brought something out from my dream.

474
00:51:07.215 --> 00:51:09.258
Where did you get that?

475
00:51:11.928 --> 00:51:13.471
I grabbed it off his head.

476
00:51:27.778 --> 00:51:31.030
Donald. she said she grabbed it
off his head in her dream.

477
00:51:31.198 --> 00:51:32.740
No. I'm not crazy.

478
00:51:32.908 --> 00:51:35.619
I'm holding the damn thing
right here in my hand.

479
00:51:35.787 --> 00:51:40.083
I don't know where she really found it.
I gotta go.

480
00:51:51.345 --> 00:51:54.264
You didn't sleep at all last night.
did you?

481
00:51:55.766 --> 00:51:59.644
- The doctor says you have to sleep. or...
- I'll go even crazier?

482
00:51:59.812 --> 00:52:04.566
I don't think you're crazy.
and stop drinking that damn coffee.

483
00:52:08.155 --> 00:52:12.450
So did you ask Daddy
to have the hat examined?

484
00:52:12.868 --> 00:52:15.995
I threw that filthy thing away.

485
00:52:16.496 --> 00:52:19.457
I don't know where you found it
or what you're trying to prove...

486
00:52:19.625 --> 00:52:24.045
What I learned in the dream clinic.
that's what I'm trying to prove. Mother.

487
00:52:24.630 --> 00:52:29.300
Rod didn't kill Tina.
and he didn't hang himself.

488
00:52:30.178 --> 00:52:31.763
It's this guy.

489
00:52:32.973 --> 00:52:35.308
He's after us in our dreams.

490
00:52:38.854 --> 00:52:41.314
That's just not reality. Nancy.

491
00:52:41.482 --> 00:52:43.650
It's real. Mama.

492
00:52:43.817 --> 00:52:44.943
Feel it.

493
00:52:45.653 --> 00:52:49.322
- Give me that damn thing.
- It even has his name written in it.

494
00:52:49.490 --> 00:52:51.574
Fred Krueger. Mom.

495
00:52:51.742 --> 00:52:53.826
Fred Krueger.

496
00:52:53.994 --> 00:52:57.373
Do you know who that is. Mother?
Because if you do. you better tell me...

497
00:52:57.540 --> 00:52:59.208
...because he's after me now.

498
00:52:59.376 --> 00:53:02.920
Nancy. trust your mother
for once. please.

499
00:53:03.296 --> 00:53:05.256
You'll feel better
when you get some sleep.

500
00:53:05.423 --> 00:53:07.299
Feel better?

501
00:53:07.467 --> 00:53:10.219
You call this feeling better?

502
00:53:10.845 --> 00:53:14.848
Or maybe I should grab that bottle
and veg out with you.

503
00:53:15.016 --> 00:53:18.727
Avoid everything happening to me
by just getting good and loaded.

504
00:53:26.154 --> 00:53:28.906
Fred Krueger can't come
after you. Nancy.

505
00:53:29.074 --> 00:53:33.452
He's dead. Believe me. I know.

506
00:53:33.620 --> 00:53:37.039
You knew about him all this time...

507
00:53:37.207 --> 00:53:40.543
...and you've been acting
like it was something I made up?

508
00:53:40.711 --> 00:53:43.212
Nancy. you're sick.

509
00:53:43.380 --> 00:53:46.882
There's something wrong with you.
You're imagining things.

510
00:53:47.050 --> 00:53:51.471
You'll feel better when you sleep.
It's just as simple as that.

511
00:53:51.639 --> 00:53:53.307
Screw sleep!

512
00:53:58.855 --> 00:54:01.940
Nancy. it's just a nightmare.

513
00:54:02.108 --> 00:54:04.568
That's enough.

514
00:54:13.286 --> 00:54:15.580
Whenever I get nervous. I eat.

515
00:54:15.748 --> 00:54:18.584
And if you can't do that. you sleep.

516
00:54:18.752 --> 00:54:20.711
I used to.

517
00:54:20.879 --> 00:54:22.588
Not anymore.

518
00:54:26.009 --> 00:54:29.261
Did you ever read about
the Balinese way of dreaming?

519
00:54:30.388 --> 00:54:32.556
No.

520
00:54:32.891 --> 00:54:36.268
They got this whole system
they call dream skills.

521
00:54:36.895 --> 00:54:40.856
So if you have a nightmare. for instance.
like falling. right?

522
00:54:41.024 --> 00:54:43.568
- Right.
- Well...

523
00:54:43.736 --> 00:54:46.780
...instead of screaming
and getting all nuts...

524
00:54:46.947 --> 00:54:50.116
...you say. "Okay. I'm gonna
make up my mind...

525
00:54:50.284 --> 00:54:52.118
...that I fall into a magic world."

526
00:54:52.286 --> 00:54:56.456
Make it something special
like a poem or a song.

527
00:54:57.375 --> 00:54:59.459
They get their art and literature
from dreams.

528
00:54:59.627 --> 00:55:03.380
Just wake up and write it down.
Dream skills.

529
00:55:03.547 --> 00:55:06.341
Well. what if they meet a monster
in their dreams? Then what?

530
00:55:06.509 --> 00:55:09.804
They turn their back on it.
Take away its energy and it disappears.

531
00:55:11.306 --> 00:55:13.141
But what happens
if they don't do that?

532
00:55:14.477 --> 00:55:17.312
Well. I guess those people
don't wake up to tell what happens.

533
00:55:17.480 --> 00:55:19.147
Great.

534
00:55:22.944 --> 00:55:25.695
"Booby Traps and lmprovised
Anti-personnel Devices"?

535
00:55:27.365 --> 00:55:29.074
Well. what are you reading that for?

536
00:55:30.326 --> 00:55:32.577
I'm into survival.

537
00:55:33.539 --> 00:55:37.250
- See you.
- You're starting to scare me.

538
00:55:48.178 --> 00:55:50.555
Oh. gross.

539
00:56:19.545 --> 00:56:21.379
Mother!

540
00:56:26.219 --> 00:56:27.928
What's with the bars?

541
00:56:30.223 --> 00:56:32.641
- Security.
- Security?

542
00:56:32.809 --> 00:56:37.313
- Security from what?
- Not from what. from whom.

543
00:56:39.983 --> 00:56:42.776
Come down to the cellar with me
and I'll tell you.

544
00:57:03.967 --> 00:57:06.302
You wanna know who Fred Krueger was?

545
00:57:07.262 --> 00:57:11.891
He was a filthy child murderer who killed
at least 20 kids in the neighborhood.

546
00:57:12.518 --> 00:57:13.684
Kids we all knew.

547
00:57:15.812 --> 00:57:17.564
Oh. Mom.

548
00:57:18.233 --> 00:57:20.943
It drove us crazy
when we didn't know who it was...

549
00:57:21.110 --> 00:57:23.987
...but it was even worse
after they caught him.

550
00:57:33.248 --> 00:57:34.623
Did they put him away?

551
00:57:34.791 --> 00:57:37.417
The lawyers got fat
and the judge got famous...

552
00:57:37.585 --> 00:57:40.879
...but somebody forgot to
sign the search warrant in the right place...

553
00:57:41.047 --> 00:57:42.965
...and Krueger was free. just like that.

554
00:57:44.343 --> 00:57:45.969
What did you do. Mother?

555
00:57:47.638 --> 00:57:51.599
A bunch of us parents tracked him down
after they let him out.

556
00:57:52.434 --> 00:57:56.897
We found him in an old abandoned
boiler room where he used to take his kids.

557
00:57:58.900 --> 00:57:59.984
Go on.

558
00:58:01.778 --> 00:58:03.862
We took gasoline...

559
00:58:04.698 --> 00:58:09.619
...we poured it all around the place
and made a trail of it out the door...

560
00:58:10.663 --> 00:58:13.873
...then lit the whole thing up
and watched it burn.

561
00:58:20.840 --> 00:58:23.466
But he can't get you now.

562
00:58:24.468 --> 00:58:27.387
He's dead. honey.
because Mommy killed him.

563
00:58:30.600 --> 00:58:32.767
I even took his knives.

564
00:58:42.195 --> 00:58:43.487
So it's okay now.

565
00:58:46.658 --> 00:58:49.118
You can sleep.

566
00:58:59.881 --> 00:59:01.381
- Hello.
- Hi.

567
00:59:01.549 --> 00:59:05.053
- Oh. hi. how you doing?
- Fine.

568
00:59:05.220 --> 00:59:08.598
Stand by your window so I can see you.
You sound a million miles away.

569
00:59:13.937 --> 00:59:15.063
That's much better.

570
00:59:15.898 --> 00:59:18.566
I see your mom went ape
at the security store today.

571
00:59:18.734 --> 00:59:20.652
You look like the Prisoner of Zenda.

572
00:59:20.819 --> 00:59:24.280
- How long's it been since you slept?
- It's coming up on the seventh day.

573
00:59:24.740 --> 00:59:27.492
It's okay. I checked Guinness.
The record's 11.

574
00:59:28.495 --> 00:59:31.246
Listen. Glen. I know who he is.

575
00:59:31.414 --> 00:59:33.457
- Who?
- The killer.

576
00:59:33.625 --> 00:59:35.084
- You do?
- Yes.

577
00:59:35.585 --> 00:59:37.878
And if he gets me.
I'm pretty sure you're next.

578
00:59:38.046 --> 00:59:40.339
Me? Why would anybody wanna kill me?

579
00:59:40.507 --> 00:59:44.218
Don't ask.
Just give me some help nailing the guy...

580
00:59:44.386 --> 00:59:45.594
...when I bring him out.

581
00:59:46.013 --> 00:59:48.682
- Bring him out of what?
- My dream.

582
00:59:50.434 --> 00:59:52.936
- How do you plan to do that?
- Just like I did the hat.

583
00:59:53.104 --> 00:59:55.439
Have a hold of the sucker
when you wake me up.

584
00:59:56.149 --> 00:59:57.525
What...? Wait a minute.

585
00:59:57.693 --> 00:59:59.527
You can't bring somebody
out of a dream.

586
00:59:59.695 --> 01:00:03.989
If I can't. then you can all relax.
because it's just a case of me being nuts.

587
01:00:04.157 --> 01:00:07.451
Yeah. well. I can save you the trouble.
You're nutty as a fruitcake.

588
01:00:07.619 --> 01:00:10.663
- I love you anyway.
- Good.

589
01:00:11.123 --> 01:00:14.291
Then you won't mind cold-cocking this guy
when I bring him out.

590
01:00:14.459 --> 01:00:16.502
- What?
- You heard me.

591
01:00:16.670 --> 01:00:20.340
I grab the guy in my dream.
You see me struggling. so you wake me up.

592
01:00:20.508 --> 01:00:23.510
We both come out. you whack the fucker.
and we got him.

593
01:00:23.678 --> 01:00:25.429
Are you crazy? Hit him with what?

594
01:00:25.596 --> 01:00:28.807
You're the jock.
You have a baseball bat or something.

595
01:00:30.435 --> 01:00:33.061
Just meet me at my porch at midnight.

596
01:00:33.229 --> 01:00:36.022
- Oh. and meanwhile...
- Meanwhile?

597
01:00:36.566 --> 01:00:41.571
Whatever you do. don't fall asleep.

598
01:00:45.117 --> 01:00:46.744
Midnight?

599
01:00:56.171 --> 01:00:58.088
Oh. man.

600
01:00:58.256 --> 01:00:59.882
Midnight.

601
01:01:00.049 --> 01:01:02.301
Baseball bats and boogeymen.

602
01:01:03.511 --> 01:01:05.262
Beautiful.

603
01:01:31.707 --> 01:01:34.584
Glen. Honey?

604
01:01:36.546 --> 01:01:38.715
Glen.

605
01:01:41.636 --> 01:01:43.595
Glen. Glen.

606
01:01:46.974 --> 01:01:50.727
How can you listen to television
and hear your records at the same time?

607
01:01:51.312 --> 01:01:54.564
Oh. I wasn't listening to the tube. Ma.
Just watching.

608
01:01:54.732 --> 01:01:57.108
Miss Nude America
is gonna be on tonight.

609
01:01:57.860 --> 01:02:01.571
- How can you hear what she's going to say?
- Who cares what she says?

610
01:02:02.281 --> 01:02:04.325
Don't be such a smart guy.

611
01:02:04.493 --> 01:02:08.538
I want you to go to bed.
It's almost midnight.

612
01:02:08.705 --> 01:02:11.958
Goodness knows we've all
had a lot to deal with these last few days.

613
01:02:12.125 --> 01:02:17.421
- I will. Mom. You guys turning in?
- Pretty soon. Now get to bed.

614
01:02:28.183 --> 01:02:32.063
It's over now. baby.
The nightmare's over.

615
01:02:32.231 --> 01:02:33.940
Please.

616
01:02:35.442 --> 01:02:37.402
Okay.

617
01:03:54.692 --> 01:03:56.944
You shouldn't stare.

618
01:03:57.904 --> 01:03:59.947
You know what I think?

619
01:04:00.114 --> 01:04:03.325
I think that kid is some kind of lunatic
or something.

620
01:04:03.493 --> 01:04:08.080
Oh. you shouldn't talk that way
about that poor child.

621
01:04:08.247 --> 01:04:10.374
You mean those bars?

622
01:04:10.541 --> 01:04:14.504
Marge is just being cautious.
what with her being all alone...

623
01:04:14.672 --> 01:04:19.218
...and Nancy acting so nervous lately.

624
01:04:19.386 --> 01:04:20.886
I don't care what you say.

625
01:04:21.054 --> 01:04:24.306
I don't want that kid
hanging around with our son anymore.

626
01:05:14.777 --> 01:05:16.695
Glen. answer the phone.

627
01:05:18.656 --> 01:05:20.282
Hello.

628
01:05:23.453 --> 01:05:27.956
Just a minute. It's her.
She wants to talk to Glen.

629
01:05:28.124 --> 01:05:30.000
About what?

630
01:05:30.460 --> 01:05:33.296
What's this about. Nancy?

631
01:05:34.506 --> 01:05:36.132
Just a minute.

632
01:05:36.300 --> 01:05:41.345
She says it's private. very private
and very important.

633
01:05:41.513 --> 01:05:44.974
Give me that. Glen's asleep.
You'll have to talk to him tomorrow.

634
01:05:45.142 --> 01:05:48.102
You've just gotta be firm
with these kids. that's all. Let's go.

635
01:05:48.270 --> 01:05:50.313
As a matter of fact...

636
01:06:00.825 --> 01:06:02.493
Damn.

637
01:06:05.121 --> 01:06:10.752
Glen. Don't fall asleep.

638
01:06:21.514 --> 01:06:23.056
Glen?

639
01:06:28.355 --> 01:06:30.439
No!

640
01:06:34.569 --> 01:06:36.695
Oh. brilliant.

641
01:06:38.031 --> 01:06:41.158
What if Glen tries to call?

642
01:07:14.862 --> 01:07:18.740
- Hello.
- I'm your boyfriend now. Nancy.

643
01:07:30.295 --> 01:07:32.504
My boyfriend.

644
01:07:39.137 --> 01:07:44.100
- Mom!
- Locked. locked. locked. locked.

645
01:07:44.268 --> 01:07:47.228
I locked it all up. I had to.

646
01:07:47.396 --> 01:07:52.108
Nancy. you are going to
get some sleep tonight if it kills me.

647
01:07:52.276 --> 01:07:55.111
Give me the key. Mother.

648
01:07:55.279 --> 01:07:59.116
I can't. I don't even have it on me. See?

649
01:07:59.284 --> 01:08:00.284
Damn it!

650
01:08:08.753 --> 01:08:10.629
ANNOuNCER:
It is now 12 midnight...

651
01:08:10.796 --> 01:08:15.175
...and this is Station KRGR
leaving the air.

652
01:08:18.930 --> 01:08:24.226
No! No! No! Ma!

653
01:08:29.023 --> 01:08:32.317
Glen! Glen!

654
01:09:05.437 --> 01:09:08.606
Come on. Frankie.
Give me a hand. Come on.

655
01:09:10.192 --> 01:09:13.403
You won't need a stretcher up there.
You'll need a mop.

656
01:09:16.031 --> 01:09:18.449
Let's go. Let's go.

657
01:09:20.953 --> 01:09:22.578
Hey!

658
01:09:24.206 --> 01:09:25.832
Don't tell me it's another one.

659
01:09:26.000 --> 01:09:27.710
Lieutenant. I'm sorry to wake you...

660
01:09:27.877 --> 01:09:30.212
...but I've never seen anything
like this before...

661
01:09:30.380 --> 01:09:33.799
...and this is your neighborhood.
so I thought I'd better call right away.

662
01:09:33.967 --> 01:09:36.719
The coroner's upstairs now.
but I don't think he's gonna...

663
01:09:51.986 --> 01:09:53.904
Would have woke me up.

664
01:09:55.949 --> 01:09:57.992
Oh. my God.

665
01:09:59.244 --> 01:10:01.704
Hello? Huh?

666
01:10:01.872 --> 01:10:03.748
Yeah. I'll get him right away.

667
01:10:04.583 --> 01:10:06.876
Lieutenant. it's your daughter.

668
01:10:15.135 --> 01:10:18.513
- Nancy.
- Hi. Daddy.

669
01:10:19.307 --> 01:10:23.226
- I know what happened.
- I haven't been upstairs yet.

670
01:10:23.394 --> 01:10:26.063
Yeah. but you know he's dead. right?

671
01:10:26.230 --> 01:10:28.315
Yeah. Apparently he's dead.

672
01:10:30.234 --> 01:10:33.737
Listen. Daddy.
I've got a proposition for you.

673
01:10:34.530 --> 01:10:37.324
- Listen very carefully. please.
- Nancy.

674
01:10:37.492 --> 01:10:40.036
I'm gonna go
and get the guy who did it...

675
01:10:41.080 --> 01:10:44.457
...and I want you to be there to arrest him
when I bring him out. okay?

676
01:10:44.626 --> 01:10:46.794
Just tell me who did it.
I'll go get him. baby.

677
01:10:48.088 --> 01:10:51.507
Fred Krueger did it. Daddy.
and only I can get him.

678
01:10:51.674 --> 01:10:54.468
It's my nightmare he comes to.

679
01:10:54.636 --> 01:10:59.973
Just come here and break the door down
in exactly 20 minutes.

680
01:11:00.141 --> 01:11:03.143
- Can you do that?
- Yeah. sure.

681
01:11:03.311 --> 01:11:07.022
That'll be exactly half past midnight.

682
01:11:08.858 --> 01:11:12.695
Time... Time enough for me
to fall asleep and find him.

683
01:11:12.863 --> 01:11:15.448
Honey. look. you just do that.
Get yourself some sleep.

684
01:11:15.616 --> 01:11:18.493
- That's what I've been telling you.
- But you'll be here?

685
01:11:18.661 --> 01:11:22.122
- They're waiting for you upstairs.
- Yeah. Sure. I'll be there. sweetheart.

686
01:11:22.289 --> 01:11:26.251
Now. look. you just get yourself
some rest. please. Deal?

687
01:11:26.419 --> 01:11:29.421
- Deal.
- I love you. sweetheart.

688
01:11:32.716 --> 01:11:36.011
Look. go outside
and watch my daughter's house.

689
01:11:36.179 --> 01:11:39.474
- lf you see anything funny. call me.
- Anything funny? Like what?

690
01:11:39.642 --> 01:11:43.812
I don't know. One thing for sure.
I don't want her coming over here.

691
01:11:43.980 --> 01:11:46.940
She's too far gone
to be able to handle this.

692
01:13:05.690 --> 01:13:09.985
- What the hell did that. lieutenant?
- I don't know.

693
01:13:10.153 --> 01:13:14.990
- What's the coroner got to say?
- He's in the john puking since he saw it.

694
01:13:18.954 --> 01:13:22.165
I guess I should have
told you about him then.

695
01:13:23.084 --> 01:13:26.546
Let's just get some sleep. Mom.
It's gonna be okay.

696
01:13:26.713 --> 01:13:29.715
I was just trying to protect you.

697
01:13:30.551 --> 01:13:33.678
I didn't see
how much you needed to know.

698
01:13:35.764 --> 01:13:40.309
You face things. That's your nature.

699
01:13:40.477 --> 01:13:41.894
That's your gift...

700
01:13:43.647 --> 01:13:46.691
...but sometime
you have to turn away too.

701
01:13:58.621 --> 01:13:59.913
I love you.

702
01:14:04.252 --> 01:14:06.169
I love you too. baby.

703
01:14:21.021 --> 01:14:22.521
Night.

704
01:14:27.569 --> 01:14:30.070
Okay. Krueger.

705
01:14:30.905 --> 01:14:32.906
We play in your court.

706
01:14:48.591 --> 01:14:53.094
And now I lay me down to sleep.
I pray the Lord my soul to keep...

707
01:14:53.262 --> 01:15:00.060
...and if I die before I wake.
I pray the Lord my soul to take.

708
01:15:03.606 --> 01:15:07.318
AuTOMATED VOICE: Countdown mode.
Ten minutes and counting.

709
01:15:20.208 --> 01:15:23.001
What if they meet a monster
in their dreams? Then what?

710
01:15:23.169 --> 01:15:26.296
They turn their back on it.
Take away its energy and it disappears.

711
01:15:26.464 --> 01:15:28.298
But what happens if they don't do that?

712
01:15:28.466 --> 01:15:31.719
Well. then I guess those people
don't wake up to tell what happens.

713
01:16:48.968 --> 01:16:51.636
Nancy.

714
01:17:00.521 --> 01:17:03.816
You dreamed about the same creep I did.

715
01:17:04.860 --> 01:17:07.445
Gonna get you.

716
01:17:15.747 --> 01:17:20.584
No! No! No!

717
01:17:28.384 --> 01:17:31.053
Nancy.

718
01:18:06.424 --> 01:18:08.552
Krueger!

719
01:18:11.222 --> 01:18:13.181
I'm here!

720
01:19:59.127 --> 01:20:03.547
Come out and show yourself.
you bastard!

721
01:20:08.261 --> 01:20:09.804
Shit.

722
01:20:14.101 --> 01:20:16.352
Come on. Krueger! Follow me!

723
01:20:22.860 --> 01:20:24.820
Damn it!

724
01:20:25.697 --> 01:20:27.906
Where are you?

725
01:20:28.157 --> 01:20:30.951
Where are you. Krueger?

726
01:20:31.619 --> 01:20:34.413
I know you're here.

727
01:20:35.498 --> 01:20:38.250
AuTOMATED VOICE:
Final 10 seconds.

728
01:20:38.418 --> 01:20:40.420
Nine. eight. seven. six...

729
01:20:40.587 --> 01:20:42.255
Nancy.

730
01:20:44.467 --> 01:20:47.386
I got you now!

731
01:21:16.125 --> 01:21:18.960
I'm crazy after all.

732
01:21:32.099 --> 01:21:34.018
It's on. Krueger!

733
01:21:34.186 --> 01:21:37.773
Take it down! Come and get me!

734
01:21:40.151 --> 01:21:42.360
Help! I've got him! Hey. Daddy!

735
01:21:42.528 --> 01:21:46.364
I've got him trapped!
Help! Where are you?

736
01:21:46.532 --> 01:21:50.327
Everything's gonna be all right!
Everything's under control!

737
01:21:50.495 --> 01:21:52.913
Get my dad. you asshole!

738
01:21:56.584 --> 01:21:58.585
Daddy!

739
01:22:03.050 --> 01:22:05.760
Come on! He's in here!

740
01:22:05.928 --> 01:22:07.720
Don't let him kill me too!

741
01:22:23.195 --> 01:22:25.404
Come on. Freddy. Can't you catch me?

742
01:22:28.452 --> 01:22:30.578
I'm gonna split you in two.

743
01:22:38.546 --> 01:22:42.298
Help! Daddy. help me. please!

744
01:22:42.716 --> 01:22:44.551
Maybe I better go tell the lieutenant.

745
01:22:55.105 --> 01:22:57.898
I'll kill you slow.

746
01:23:00.902 --> 01:23:02.903
Now. where are you?

747
01:23:03.071 --> 01:23:04.572
Hey!

748
01:23:05.115 --> 01:23:09.326
No! No. no! No!

749
01:23:36.940 --> 01:23:40.276
Daddy. I did it! Please hurry!

750
01:23:41.153 --> 01:23:43.070
Daddy!

751
01:23:43.238 --> 01:23:45.490
Where are you?

752
01:23:48.036 --> 01:23:50.078
Parker. I need some help here!

753
01:23:50.246 --> 01:23:53.373
Okay. you guys. Come on. let's go.
Let's go. Al. Jim. get over here.

754
01:23:53.541 --> 01:23:56.126
- Nancy!
- Daddy!

755
01:23:56.294 --> 01:23:58.754
- Daddy!
- Get you out.

756
01:23:58.922 --> 01:24:02.257
- Open the door!
- Watch yourself. lieutenant.

757
01:24:02.425 --> 01:24:03.467
I got it.

758
01:24:03.635 --> 01:24:06.511
- Dad. it's Krueger!
- Get out of the way.

759
01:24:08.431 --> 01:24:10.057
Nancy.

760
01:24:12.311 --> 01:24:14.270
This way. guys. Come down here.

761
01:24:14.438 --> 01:24:17.148
- What the hell came through here?
- As if I know.

762
01:24:17.316 --> 01:24:18.651
Oh. my God.

763
01:24:18.818 --> 01:24:20.778
Nancy. what the hell is going on?

764
01:24:20.946 --> 01:24:22.571
Parker. get up here!

765
01:24:22.739 --> 01:24:27.034
- We got a fire up here too.
- Okay. yeah. we're on our way up.

766
01:24:29.829 --> 01:24:32.248
What the hell is going on. Nancy?

767
01:24:32.415 --> 01:24:34.375
He's after Mother!

768
01:24:46.138 --> 01:24:49.849
Daddy! Watch out! He's under there!

769
01:25:07.703 --> 01:25:11.747
Mother! Mother. Mother!

770
01:25:16.754 --> 01:25:18.422
Now do you believe me?

771
01:25:19.132 --> 01:25:21.758
They've got the fires out downstairs.

772
01:25:21.926 --> 01:25:23.885
Everything okay up here?

773
01:25:34.773 --> 01:25:36.816
I'm okay.

774
01:25:38.402 --> 01:25:40.862
You go downstairs.

775
01:25:41.030 --> 01:25:43.698
I'll be there in a minute.

776
01:25:47.578 --> 01:25:49.495
Lieutenant. is everything all right?

777
01:25:49.663 --> 01:25:52.206
I don't know. I don't know.

778
01:26:24.326 --> 01:26:25.868
I know you're there. Freddy.

779
01:26:30.791 --> 01:26:33.667
You think you was
gonna get away from me?

780
01:26:33.835 --> 01:26:36.045
I know you too well now. Freddy.

781
01:26:38.048 --> 01:26:40.841
Now you die.

782
01:26:42.677 --> 01:26:44.970
It's too late. Krueger.

783
01:26:45.138 --> 01:26:47.933
I know the secret now.

784
01:26:48.309 --> 01:26:52.854
This is just a dream. You're not alive.

785
01:26:53.022 --> 01:26:56.733
This whole thing is just a dream.

786
01:26:58.986 --> 01:27:01.155
I want my mother and friends again.

787
01:27:01.740 --> 01:27:03.074
You what?

788
01:27:03.784 --> 01:27:07.829
I take back every bit of energy
I gave you.

789
01:27:09.081 --> 01:27:10.998
You're nothing.

790
01:27:13.502 --> 01:27:14.545
You're shit.

791
01:27:27.517 --> 01:27:29.393
God.

792
01:27:30.562 --> 01:27:32.813
It's bright.

793
01:27:34.899 --> 01:27:37.401
It's gonna burn off soon.
or it wouldn't be so bright.

794
01:27:37.861 --> 01:27:41.531
- Feeling better?
- Oh. I feel like a million bucks.

795
01:27:41.699 --> 01:27:45.660
They say you've bottomed out
when you can't remember the night before.

796
01:27:45.828 --> 01:27:50.790
You know. baby. I'm gonna stop drinking.
I just don't feel like it anymore.

797
01:27:50.958 --> 01:27:53.084
Did I keep you awake last night?

798
01:27:53.252 --> 01:27:55.963
You look a little bit peaked.

799
01:27:56.214 --> 01:28:00.509
No. I guess I just slept heavy.

800
01:28:01.052 --> 01:28:04.472
Okay. I'll see you.

801
01:28:04.639 --> 01:28:06.349
See you.

802
01:28:09.854 --> 01:28:11.480
- Stop it.
- Hi. everybody.

803
01:28:11.647 --> 01:28:16.067
- You believe this fog?
- Oh. I believe anything is possible.

804
01:28:16.235 --> 01:28:19.029
- Bye.
- Looking good. girl.

805
01:28:19.197 --> 01:28:21.990
- Hey!
- What happened?

806
01:28:23.576 --> 01:28:25.243
What's going on?

807
01:28:25.912 --> 01:28:28.872
- Hey. Hey. I'm not doing this.
- Glen! Let us out!

808
01:28:29.040 --> 01:28:31.541
- I'm not doing this.
- What's going on with the window?

809
01:28:31.709 --> 01:28:33.586
No. Mother!

810
01:28:34.254 --> 01:28:40.259
- Mother! Mother! Mother!
- What's going on?

811
01:28:44.556 --> 01:28:49.268
One. two
Freddy's coming for you

812
01:28:54.442 --> 01:28:59.364
Three. four
Better lock your door

813
01:28:59.532 --> 01:29:04.619
Five. six
Grab your crucifix

814
01:29:05.454 --> 01:29:10.667
Seven. eight
Gonna stay up late

815
01:29:10.834 --> 01:29:17.632
Nine. ten
Never sleep again

